+"""OCT intensity-normalisation options for the prep (v1.2 candidates after the P11 probe:norm on I58).
+
+prep_subject.py keeps the frozen v1 ``common.oct_slab_normalize`` on its default path (per-slice tissue median along array
+axis 0 at the native resolution).  This module adds, behind prep flags:
+
+  slab_normalize             the same v1 algorithm along ANY array axis, or a global gain only (``gain_only``), with an absolute
+                             (v1: 1e-3) or relative (1e-3 x median of the per-slice medians) floor on the per-slice median
+  plane_normalize_inplace    per-plane median normalisation of the vessel-level volume along one axis (the detected sectioning
+                             axis; applied after the destripe, window 1.2 mm = 4 sections on I58)
+  tile_flatfield_inplace     2-D folded multiplicative flat field of the tile mosaic on the two en-face axes (the axes other than
+                             the sectioning axis), constant along the sectioning axis
+  level150_from_octv         prep's 0.15 mm level from a vessel-level volume (block means + resample), for scripts/renorm_prep.py
+
+P11 (I58, docs in the probe record): the prep's axis-0 correction is 1.5 % (std of log scale) and 85 % of its power sits at the
+2.82 mm tile harmonics; the tile mosaic has fundamentals 70.44 / 69.72 voxels at 40 um on axes 0 / 1 with a non-separable 2-D fold
+(log std 1.2-1.5 %, p2p 8-10 %) that flips about 1 % of the WM/GM class voxels.  None of the variants changed the structural
+objective at P_R5 by more than 0.0004 NCC, so on I58 these options are registration-neutral; they exist for a physically
+motivated prep and must go through the DANDI regression before any default changes.  What the probe ruled out as the source of the
+axis-0 stretch preference is only these small corrections (axis-0 per-slice correction, axis-2 section normalisation, tile field; log
+std <= 0.015); the kept axis-0 trend (std log 0.126) and the global gain were never varied.  The global tile field assumes one tile
+phase for the whole block: sections whose mosaic is shifted by a tile step get a larger tile amplitude from it (P11 I58: section groups
+0-2), which the section-group diagnostics of tile_flatfield_inplace report and group_mode 'per_group' avoids.
+
+Conventions: volumes are (Z,Y,X) arrays (ndarray or memmap); zeros are missing data (black tiles) and stay exactly zero; float16
+outputs are clipped to [1, CAP_F16] on valid voxels like octreg.destripe.  All functions are CPU/numpy except level150_from_octv."""
+from __future__ import annotations
